#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:1
msgid "Hunspell Setup"
msgstr "Hunspell Setup"

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:3
msgid "Harper reads English. LanguageTool reads about forty languages. Hunspell fills what is left — Hebrew, Latin, Welsh, Old English, and a long tail besides — using the dictionary format that LibreOffice, Firefox and every desktop spell checker already use."
msgstr "Harper reads English. LanguageTool reads about forty languages. Hunspell fills what is left — Hebrew, Latin, Welsh, Old English, and a long tail besides — using the dictionary format that LibreOffice, Firefox and every desktop spell checker already use."

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:8
msgid "It checks spelling and nothing else. There are no grammar rules here, so a language served by Hunspell alone gets a narrower check than one LanguageTool supports. Where both are available, prefer LanguageTool."
msgstr "It checks spelling and nothing else. There are no grammar rules here, so a language served by Hunspell alone gets a narrower check than one LanguageTool supports. Where both are available, prefer LanguageTool."

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:12
msgid "Why dictionaries are not bundled"
msgstr "Why dictionaries are not bundled"

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:14
msgid "Language Check ships no dictionaries and cannot. Hspell, which supplies Hebrew, is AGPL-3.0; the Latin dictionary is GPL. Neither belongs inside an MIT binary published to crates.io and the VS Code Marketplace."
msgstr "Language Check ships no dictionaries and cannot. Hspell, which supplies Hebrew, is AGPL-3.0; the Latin dictionary is GPL. Neither belongs inside an MIT binary published to crates.io and the VS Code Marketplace."

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:18
msgid "They are installed separately instead, into your own data directory, under their own licenses — the same arrangement VS Code, Firefox and LibreOffice use for the same reason. The installer states a dictionary's license and where its words came from before fetching anything."
msgstr "They are installed separately instead, into your own data directory, under their own licenses — the same arrangement VS Code, Firefox and LibreOffice use for the same reason. The installer states a dictionary's license and where its words came from before fetching anything."

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:23
msgid "Enabling it"
msgstr "Enabling it"

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:32
msgid "`languages` names the tags Hunspell answers for. Naming them is what keeps this engine to the gaps: leave English out and Harper keeps it. An empty list means \"any language with a pack behind it\", which is the discovery mode rather than the tidy one."
msgstr "`languages` names the tags Hunspell answers for. Naming them is what keeps this engine to the gaps: leave English out and Harper keeps it. An empty list means \"any language with a pack behind it\", which is the discovery mode rather than the tidy one."

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:37
msgid "Getting a dictionary"
msgstr "Getting a dictionary"

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:39
msgid "In the editor"
msgstr "In the editor"

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:41
msgid "Open a document declaring a language none of the enabled engines read and the extension offers to install it. Decline and it will not ask again — the offer stays available as a quick fix on the squiggle, under the lightbulb."
msgstr "Open a document declaring a language none of the enabled engines read and the extension offers to install it. Decline and it will not ask again — the offer stays available as a quick fix on the squiggle, under the lightbulb."

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:45
msgid "From the command line"
msgstr "From the command line"

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:54
msgid "From your package manager"
msgstr "From your package manager"

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:56
msgid "A pack you already have is found without downloading a second copy. On Arch:"
msgstr "A pack you already have is found without downloading a second copy. On Arch:"

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:62
msgid "Debian, Fedora, and Homebrew carry the same dictionaries under similar names."
msgstr "Debian, Fedora, and Homebrew carry the same dictionaries under similar names."

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:64
msgid "By hand"
msgstr "By hand"

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:66
msgid "Any `.aff`/`.dic` pair works. Point at it and Language Check uses that one in preference to everything else:"
msgstr "Any `.aff`/`.dic` pair works. Point at it and Language Check uses that one in preference to everything else:"

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:78
msgid "The value may be a directory, an `.aff`/`.dic` stem, or either file of the pair. This is how to use a language with no published download — Latin, for instance, ships only as a LibreOffice `.oxt` archive, so unpack it and name the directory here."
msgstr "The value may be a directory, an `.aff`/`.dic` stem, or either file of the pair. This is how to use a language with no published download — Latin, for instance, ships only as a LibreOffice `.oxt` archive, so unpack it and name the directory here."

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:83
msgid "Where packs are looked for"
msgstr "Where packs are looked for"

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:85
msgid "In order, first match winning:"
msgstr "In order, first match winning:"

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:87
msgid "`dictionary_paths`, for the language in question"
msgstr "`dictionary_paths`, for the language in question"

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:88
msgid "`search_paths`, in the order given"
msgstr "`search_paths`, in the order given"

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:89
msgid "the directory `language-check packs install` writes to"
msgstr "the directory `language-check packs install` writes to"

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:90
msgid "the platform's own: `/usr/share/hunspell`, `/usr/share/myspell`, `~/.local/share/hunspell` on Linux; `~/Library/Spelling` and `/Library/Spelling` on macOS"
msgstr "the platform's own: `/usr/share/hunspell`, `/usr/share/myspell`, `~/.local/share/hunspell` on Linux; `~/Library/Spelling` and `/Library/Spelling` on macOS"

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:94
msgid "A tag resolves to the pack it is actually shipped as, so `he` finds `he_IL`. Where several regional packs could serve one bare tag, the choice is sorted rather than whatever the directory yields, so it is the same on every machine."
msgstr "A tag resolves to the pack it is actually shipped as, so `he` finds `he_IL`. Where several regional packs could serve one bare tag, the choice is sorted rather than whatever the directory yields, so it is the same on every machine."

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:98
msgid "`language-check packs list` prints each pack and the directory it was found in."
msgstr "`language-check packs list` prints each pack and the directory it was found in."

