#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:114
msgid "What can go wrong"
msgstr "What can go wrong"

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:116
msgid "Every failure names the file and the reason, in the editor rather than only in a log."
msgstr "Every failure names the file and the reason, in the editor rather than only in a log."

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:119
msgid "**No pack for a language.** The passage is reported as unchecked instead of passing as clean, and the editor offers to install one where a download exists."
msgstr "**No pack for a language.** The passage is reported as unchecked instead of passing as clean, and the editor offers to install one where a download exists."

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:122
msgid "**A pack that will not load.** Real dictionaries carry real defects: the 2013 Latin pack has two lines reading `SFK` where `SFX` belongs, so its affix header promises 129 rows and the parser finds 2. Hunspell skips a line it does not recognize; the stricter parser here does not, which is why a pack can work in LibreOffice and fail here. `language-check packs verify <lang>` says which file and which line."
msgstr "**A pack that will not load.** Real dictionaries carry real defects: the 2013 Latin pack has two lines reading `SFK` where `SFX` belongs, so its affix header promises 129 rows and the parser finds 2. Hunspell skips a line it does not recognize; the stricter parser here does not, which is why a pack can work in LibreOffice and fail here. `language-check packs verify <lang>` says which file and which line."

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:129
msgid "**A download that does not match.** Every fetchable pack is pinned to a SHA-256 and a byte count. A download differing in either is discarded before it reaches the parser or your disk. An upstream update and a tampered mirror look identical over the wire, so both stop and say so rather than trusting what arrived — if a pack you expect starts refusing to install, that is what it means."
msgstr "**A download that does not match.** Every fetchable pack is pinned to a SHA-256 and a byte count. A download differing in either is discarded before it reaches the parser or your disk. An upstream update and a tampered mirror look identical over the wire, so both stop and say so rather than trusting what arrived — if a pack you expect starts refusing to install, that is what it means."

#: ../../guide/hunspell-setup.md:136
msgid "**No room.** Free space is checked before fetching. Hspell's Hebrew is about 8 MB."
msgstr "**No room.** Free space is checked before fetching. Hspell's Hebrew is about 8 MB."

